MADM - Notice and credits
=========================

This repository is a modern SDL2/macOS port of MADM, a simulator for the
Manchester Mark I prototype / Manchester Baby / SSEM.

Original MADM
-------------

Original simulator:

    MADM for MS-DOS
    Lee Wittenberg, 1989

The original package was distributed as `madm.zip` through the Computer
Conservation Society / Computer50 Manchester Mark I simulator archive. The
package includes Lee Wittenberg's C source code, an MS-DOS executable, a
makefile, and README.TXT.

Original README contact block:

    Lee Wittenberg
    Dept. of Mathematics and Computer Science
    Kean College of New Jersey
    Union, NJ 07083
    leew@pilot.njin.net

Port and repository
-------------------

This port updates the original C code for a modern C17 toolchain and replaces
the DOS graphics/keyboard layer with SDL2-based macOS code. The program catalog
and conversion scripts include material reconstructed from public Manchester
Baby / SSEM simulator and program archives; see `programs/README.md` and
`scripts/README.md` for source notes.

License status
--------------

No explicit open-source license was found in the original MADM MS-DOS package:
there is no LICENSE/COPYING file and the source headers/README do not state
redistribution or modification terms.

For that reason, this repository does not claim that the original MADM code is
available under MIT, BSD, GPL, public domain, or any other open-source license.
It is published here with attribution as a preservation-oriented port. If you
are Lee Wittenberg or a rightsholder for the original MADM code and want the
license status clarified or the repository changed, please open an issue.
